The  Ethernet  interface needs to be marked UP, but does not need
to have an IP address.  There are two basic modes  of  operation,
controlled  via  the  switch.   The  default mode, not being set,
tries to keep the configured session open all the time.   If  the
session  is disconnected, a new connection attempt is started im‐
mediately.  The mode, selected by setting only establishes a con‐
nection when data is being sent to the interface.  If the  kernel
is  compiled with options there are two modes of connection, con‐
trolled via the switch.  The default  mode,  not  being  set,  is
client mode.  The mode, selected by setting is to wait for incom‐
ing  PPPoE session.  Before a interface is usable, it needs to be
configured.  The following steps are necessary: Create the inter‐
face.  Connect an Ethernet interface.  This interface is used for
the physical communication.  As noted above it must be marked UP,
but need not have an IP address.  Configure authentication.   The
PPP  session  needs to identify the client to the peer.  For more
